2026-11-11T11:05:02.6763838Z -- v5.3.0 — defrost: duty is measured, the derate is physics
2026-11-11T11:05:02.6763954Z   ok   the inferred estimator reads a real defrost as a PERFECT interval
2026-11-11T11:05:02.6764052Z   ok   an over-1 ratio can no longer park the derate above 1.0
2026-11-11T11:05:02.6764149Z   ok   five defrosting minutes in thirty is a duty of 1/6
2026-11-11T11:05:02.6764225Z   ok   and the interval counts as observed
2026-11-11T11:05:02.6764365Z   ok   a quiet interval is duty zero AND observed — that is real evidence
2026-11-11T11:05:02.6764462Z   ok   an unreadable flag yields duty zero but NOT observed
2026-11-11T11:05:02.6764575Z   ok   a defrost spanning an interval boundary keeps its second half
2026-11-11T11:05:02.6764689Z   ok   a sample stamped before the last does not subtract from the on-time
2026-11-11T11:05:02.6764767Z   ok   zero duty is no derate at all
2026-11-11T11:05:02.6764861Z   ok   the derate is 1 - duty x the loss multiplier
2026-11-11T11:05:02.6764965Z   ok   more duty is always a deeper derate, never a shallower one
2026-11-11T11:05:02.6765076Z   ok   and it is bounded below, so a latched flag cannot zero the pump
2026-11-11T11:05:02.6765168Z   ok   a measured bucket derates from its counted duty
2026-11-11T11:05:02.6765291Z   ok   and a measurement is never averaged with an inference of the same thing
2026-11-11T11:05:02.6765374Z   ok   an untouched bucket still derates nothing
2026-11-11T11:05:02.6765549Z   ok   the summary says which estimator a bucket rests on, and how many defrosts were actually witnessed
2026-11-11T11:05:02.6765650Z   ok   a duty outside [0, 1] is refused, not folded into the bucket
2026-11-11T11:05:02.6765795Z   ok   the range guard rejects only OUTSIDE [0, 1] — 0 and 1 still fold
2026-11-11T11:05:02.6765910Z   ok   a pre-v5.3.0 store loads without raising, and says it was upgraded
