2026-11-11T11:05:02.6840253Z   ok   no topic and an offset entity: one publish of 5 sends one set_value of 5 (R10-GENERIC-HEAT-CURVE)
2026-11-11T11:05:02.6840504Z   ok   the entity option empty: no set_value, and the /set topic still carries the integer (W7)
2026-11-11T11:05:02.6840778Z   ok   both configured: MQTT first with the full integer, the entity bounded by the 3 K default band
2026-11-11T11:05:02.6840973Z   ok   a kelvin entity is sent -2 for -2, never 271.15 through the absolute helpers (T1)
2026-11-11T11:05:02.6841126Z   ok   a Fahrenheit entity is sent the difference x9/5: 2 K is 3.6 °F (T1)
2026-11-11T11:05:02.6841286Z   ok   an entity range narrower than the displace saturates and is latched once, naming it (W6)
2026-11-11T11:05:02.6841385Z   ok   a reading already at the target is not written (W1)
2026-11-11T11:05:02.6841515Z   ok   inside the grace a differing reading proves nothing: no second write (W2)
2026-11-11T11:05:02.6841621Z   ok   after the grace the first miss is written once more (W2)
2026-11-11T11:05:02.6841754Z   ok   a second miss for the same target latches a warning and sends nothing (W3)
2026-11-11T11:05:02.6841830Z   ok   and a new target is written again (W3)
2026-11-11T11:05:02.6841954Z   ok   the 24 h write guard is 2 x 1440 / interval: 96 at the default 30 min (W4)
2026-11-11T11:05:02.6842100Z   ok   at the guard nothing is written and it is latched; one below it the write goes (W4)
2026-11-11T11:05:02.6842389Z   ok   absent, unavailable, a non-temperature unit, a sensor, a range without 0 or a raising service: no value lands, the failure is latched, the MQTT arm still publishes
2026-11-11T11:05:02.6842483Z   ok   MODE_OFF after a write writes one 0 (the off rule)
2026-11-11T11:05:02.6842592Z   ok   and while off the arm writes nothing, nor does a second off
2026-11-11T11:05:02.6842728Z   ok   nothing written, nothing restored; an unconfigured entity is never written
2026-11-11T11:05:02.6842858Z   ok   unload after a write writes one 0, through async_unload_entry (the off rule)
2026-11-11T11:05:02.6842980Z   ok   a write left armed by a crash is restored by the next run's first off
2026-11-11T11:05:02.6843264Z   ok   a stand-in second consumer registers without editing the hook: its baseline, captured before its first write, survives a restart and is what the restore writes
2026-11-11T11:05:02.6843404Z   ok   and an unreadable baseline refuses the consumer's write: nothing to restore it to
2026-11-11T11:05:02.6843608Z   ok   an unregistered consumer, or one its factory reads as unconfigured, refuses the write and leaves no record behind
2026-11-11T11:05:02.6843779Z   ok   a restore whose write raises sends nothing, stays armed and latches a warning naming the entity
2026-11-11T11:05:02.6844047Z   ok   and the next off retries it: one write of the neutral 0, disarmed and counted
2026-11-11T11:05:02.6844290Z   ok   an armed consumer no longer configured is disarmed unwritten: its entity is not the optimizer's
2026-11-11T11:05:02.6844451Z   ok   a store that cannot save still arms the write, and one that cannot be removed does not raise
2026-11-11T11:05:02.6844633Z   ok   T2 at its bounds: a range starting or ending at 0 is an offset, one starting at 0.5 or ending at -0.5 is not
2026-11-11T11:05:02.6844765Z   ok   every refusal of the pure convert names why and is never read as saturated
2026-11-11T11:05:02.6844916Z   ok   a range narrower than the displace saturates on the low side too: -3 K sends -2 (W6)
2026-11-11T11:05:02.6845092Z   ok   a reading exactly half a step from the target holds: 2.25 against 2 at step 0.5 is not written (W1)
2026-11-11T11:05:02.6845292Z   ok   a target within half a step of the last write is that write, still in its grace: 3 after 2 at step 2 sends nothing (W2)
2026-11-11T11:05:02.6845518Z   ok   a reading that held clears the misses, and the grace is 90 s: a miss 91 s after the write is written once more, not given up (W1, W2)
2026-11-11T11:05:02.6845681Z   ok   writes older than 24 h leave the guard: a full day of them 24 h and 1 s old blocks nothing (W4)
2026-11-11T11:05:02.6845812Z   ok   at exactly 90 s the grace is over: a miss then is written once more (W2's bound)
